; TEXTEDIT with the long name DDEDIT: the Mode option and Esc ([0.8.1-RT11], work #939;
; card PT11, point 2; ADR 0054, point 6; session of 2026-11-22).
; - Mode asks "Enter a text edit mode option [Single/Multiple] <Multiple>:"; Enter
;   keeps Multiple, then Single. As after an option of FILLET, the settings line is
;   not written again: the prompt of the Single mode has no Undo.
; - In the Single mode the command ends after one object; the mode stays for the
;   following TEXTEDIT, which writes "Edit mode = Single".
; - Esc at the object prompt and at the text prompt cancels the command, before any
;   modification: nothing changes and there is no step.
